  58:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_opt_q15.c ****  * The function is implemented using a 64-bit internal accumulator.
  59:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_opt_q15.c ****  * Both inputs are in 1.15 format and multiplications yield a 2.30 result.
  60:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_opt_q15.c ****  * The 2.30 intermediate results are accumulated in a 64-bit accumulator in 34.30 format.
  61:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_opt_q15.c ****  * This approach provides 33 guard bits and there is no risk of overflow.
  62:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_opt_q15.c ****  * The 34.30 result is then truncated to 34.15 format by discarding the low 15 bits and then satura
  63:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_opt_q15.c ****  *
  64:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_opt_q15.c ****  * \par
  65:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_opt_q15.c ****  * Refer to <code>arm_correlate_fast_q15()</code> for a faster but less precise version of this fun
  66:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_opt_q15.c ****  *
